     "claim": "A_hook",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "Ethan Couch, 16, driving drunk, killed four people in a crash in Burleson, Texas, on 15 June 2013; in December 2013 he was sentenced (juvenile court) to ten years' probation with no jail or prison time. Narration: 'He killed four people. He got no prison.' Headline: '4 DEAD. NO PRISON.'",
     "urls": [
      "https://okcfox.com/archive/texas-teen-gets-10-years-probation-for-driving-drunk-killing-4",
      "https://fox13now.com/2013/12/11/texas-teen-ethan-couch-gets-10-years-probation-for-driving-drunk-killing-4/",
      "https://www.cbsnews.com/texas/news/deadly-drunk-driving-probation-sentence-leaves-families-stunned",
      "https://www.slate.com/blogs/the_slatest/2013/12/12/ethan_couch_affluenza_texas_teen_spared_prison_time_in_deadly_drunk_driving.html",
      "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethan_Couch",
      "https://okcfox.com/archive/judge-orders-texas-affluenza-teen-to-rehab-for-driving-drunk-killing-4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "claim": "A_affluenza",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "The defense presented a psychologist who said Couch was a product of 'affluenza' (a privileged, permissive upbringing). Narration: 'His defense? He grew up too rich.' (the hot-take framing of 'affluenza'; the next scene states the testimony). The judge did not say affluenza was the basis of her decision (recorded, see A_judge).",
     "urls": [
      "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethan_Couch",
